Tomorrow was a big day.  Your first lecture of the semester.  It was
a new class, a fresh beginning, and it was going to feel good, being
on stage.  Five years of grudging university work, getting through
that PhD, facing the panel and defending your thesis, and then
finally the decision to return to Pakistan and help your country. 

Your parents had been overjoyed, but also worried. And after the
news today, you understood that feeling. How long before the very
students and university you joined figured out your religious
affiliations? How long before that became a problem? 

It was impossible to tell. And yet you were still excited, buoyed up
by the enthusiasm of youth, the belief that it couldn't really
happen to you. 

And with that thought, you get up and head to bed. 


