SEVENTH ROOM

Climax. 

You get fired from the job, on a false charge of 'spreading
propaganda' in your classes, although to the best of your knowledge
the only thing you've taught up til now has been theoretical
physics. 


You go home to find your worried parents telling you Kashifa has
broken off the engagement. 

Police arrive in the evening, to 'investigate' the charges. Your
accounts have been frozen. After a gruelling week in jail, you are
finally released, to go home without a job, without any money,
without a fiance. Your parents are half dead from grief, your sister
has been expelled from college. 

You can barely stand to see yourself in the mirror. With no money,
there is no chance of even escaping abroad again. And what about
your parents? Your brother and sister? there was no escape even for
them. There was no escape anywhere. 

In a fog of depression, you decide to end it all. 
